(5889182, 858007, 61961, '<td valign="top">Good concept, but needs a lot of help photographically.  Not sure if I''m seeing camera shake or if it''s out of focus.  A shallower depth of field could blur the background, if your camera is capable (try shooting at the widest aperture (lowest aperture number); with a point and shoot you may need to increase the distance between subject and background.  You can straighten the photo using an editing program, unless the tilt is intentional</td>', 'Good concept, but needs a lot of help photographically.  Not sure if I''m seeing camera shake or if it''s out of focus.  A shallower depth of field could blur the background, if your camera is capable (try shooting at the widest aperture (lowest aperture number); with a point and shoot you may need to increase the distance between subject and background.  You can straighten the photo using an editing program, unless the tilt is intentional', '2010-03-03 17:21:45.000000', NULL, 1),
