(5897875, 858032, 108580, '<td valign="top">The Title sucked eggs. Only later did I realise it should have been called "the Babysitter"<br/>Thanks for comments and votes, for the above 5 voters who scored and looked at technicals and especially the 1 voters who didn''t think even the technicals deserved more than 1 point or didn''t see the eggs or make the correlation between the taste of chicken and the taste of frog. whahahahah. Thx also to the 177 voters who felt it was above 5, there is some hope after all!<br/>I would dearly love to have gotten comments from the 8, 9 , 10 voters as to what they like about it. <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=83313" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Yo_Spiff</a> has been struggling to get a love it/hate it shot for ages, PM me and I''ll give you some tips!<br/> <br/>@ <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=115436" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">MickiVee</a>, nope no yin yang going in when I took the shot, isn''t that the beauty of photography? <br/>@<img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=51793" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Dirt_Diver</a>, he''s guarding them and he tastes like chicken. <br/>@<img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=98339" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Ja-9</a>, those are Ostrich eggs, they are huge :) J/K<br/>@<img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=113419" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Luci11e</a> Lol indeed, it was meant to be somewhat humerous.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-03-10 11:25:05.</i></td>', 'The Title sucked eggs. Only later did I realise it should have been called "the Babysitter"Thanks for comments and votes, for the above 5 voters who scored and looked at technicals and especially the 1 voters who didn''t think even the technicals deserved more than 1 point or didn''t see the eggs or make the correlation between the taste of chicken and the taste of frog. whahahahah. Thx also to the 177 voters who felt it was above 5, there is some hope after all!I would dearly love to have gotten comments from the 8, 9 , 10 voters as to what they like about it.  Yo_Spiff has been struggling to get a love it/hate it shot for ages, PM me and I''ll give you some tips! @  MickiVee, nope no yin yang going in when I took the shot, isn''t that the beauty of photography? @ Dirt_Diver, he''s guarding them and he tastes like chicken. @ Ja-9, those are Ostrich eggs, they are huge :) J/K@ Luci11e Lol indeed, it was meant to be somewhat humerous.', '2010-03-10 01:02:24.000000', '2010-03-10 11:25:05.000000', 0),
