(5899616, 857202, 113156, '<td valign="top">I managed to destroy half a dozen eggs to get this shot, and had tedious job cleaning the chainsaw afterwards, I also tried nailing a soft boiled egg to the old barn door, it turned out ok as well so I tossed a coin to decide which one. Thanks for all the nice comments and I''m really pleased with a top ten spot.</td>', 'I managed to destroy half a dozen eggs to get this shot, and had tedious job cleaning the chainsaw afterwards, I also tried nailing a soft boiled egg to the old barn door, it turned out ok as well so I tossed a coin to decide which one. Thanks for all the nice comments and I''m really pleased with a top ten spot.', '2010-03-11 03:25:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(5899624, 858162, 10275, '<td valign="top">this is a brilliant idea</td>', 'this is a brilliant idea', '2010-03-11 03:39:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(5899730, 858094, 86218, '<td valign="top">Will never understand the voters. if I did I suppose I would score 7-8''s all the time. Although I gave this a 6 at the time I would give it a 7 now. Its something that grows on you and I suppose it did not have that immediate impact wow factor when I saw it the first time. Just viewing the shot even at first site anybody should be able to see that this is def not a 5...yet this is DPC</td>', 'Will never understand the voters. if I did I suppose I would score 7-8''s all the time. Although I gave this a 6 at the time I would give it a 7 now. Its something that grows on you and I suppose it did not have that immediate impact wow factor when I saw it the first time. Just viewing the shot even at first site anybody should be able to see that this is def not a 5...yet this is DPC', '2010-03-11 08:28:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(5899787, 858070, 52750, '<td valign="top">I remember a Frasier episode where Frasier was allowed to secretly view marketing research being conducted about his show. In a room full of people, *one* person said they didn''t like his radio show, everyone else loved it... Frasier obsessed about the one negative comment. You scored a win with a lot of people, don''t take the handful of negative comments to heart.<br/> <br/>And if we''re keeping score on originality, let''s start counting the long exposure beach scenes; pet portraits; tone-mapped portraits of old people; black and white with a splash of color; use of photos within the photo; posed mice; liquid droplets/splash photos; etc etc etc...<br/> <br/>You''re doing fine, shoot what inspires you... even if the inspiration comes while surfing the web and seeing someone else''s attempt.<br/> <br/></td>', 'I remember a Frasier episode where Frasier was allowed to secretly view marketing research being conducted about his show. In a room full of people, *one* person said they didn''t like his radio show, everyone else loved it... Frasier obsessed about the one negative comment. You scored a win with a lot of people, don''t take the handful of negative comments to heart. And if we''re keeping score on originality, let''s start counting the long exposure beach scenes; pet portraits; tone-mapped portraits of old people; black and white with a splash of color; use of photos within the photo; posed mice; liquid droplets/splash photos; etc etc etc... You''re doing fine, shoot what inspires you... even if the inspiration comes while surfing the web and seeing someone else''s attempt. ', '2010-03-11 09:30:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(5899796, 858094, 30861, '<td valign="top">Wow, 38 votes of 3 or lower? That is extraordinarily obtuse of the voters, I agree. As you put it, this wasn''t a ribbon winner, but...<br/> <br/>I don''t see why it shouldn''t have finished in the very high 5''s, I don''t see why so many thought it was so poor...<br/> <br/>I didn''t vote the challenge, but I''d have given it probably a 7.</td>', 'Wow, 38 votes of 3 or lower? That is extraordinarily obtuse of the voters, I agree. As you put it, this wasn''t a ribbon winner, but... I don''t see why it shouldn''t have finished in the very high 5''s, I don''t see why so many thought it was so poor... I didn''t vote the challenge, but I''d have given it probably a 7.', '2010-03-11 09:43:58.000000', NULL, 0),
